job_description:
**Amentum**will inspire and empower you to deliver your best work so you can evolve, grow and succeed - today and into tomorrow. We offer an exciting range of opportunities to develop your career within a supportive and diverse team who always strive to do the right thing for our people, clients and communities. People are our greatest asset, and we offer a competitive package to retain and attract the best talent. In addition to the benefits you’d expect, UK employees also receive free single medical cover and digital GP service, family-friendly benefits such as enhanced parental leave pay and free membership of employee assistance and parental programmes , plus reimbursement towards relevant professional development and memberships. We also give back to our communities through our Collectively program which incorporates matched-funding, paid volunteering time and charitable donations. **About the Opportunity**
We employ the UK's most experienced and skilled technical services professionals and has grown to over 8,000 people in locations across the UK - we provide the resources to turn great ideas into reality, and we offer capable and committed individuals the opportunity to shape their careers how they wish. Hinkley Point C (HPC) is the first new nuclear power station to be built in the UK in over 20 years, HPCs two EPR reactors will be capable of generating 3.26GW of secure, low carbon electricity for 60 years, enough electricity to power around 6 million homes. In addition to the projects ‘clean energy’ benefits, HPC will create thousands of jobs and bring lasting benefits to the UK economy.
The **Piping Engineer - Completion Lead** will deliver Mechanical & Piping Construction Work packs to support the MEH Alliance programme.
**Key Responsibilities**
* The MEH programme has commenced bulk installation on site since the start of 2024, whereas previously the focus has been on securing the design and manufacturing. As such the spotlight will fall on the construction leads for the engineering delivery of the site scope;
* The Piping Completions Lead reports functionally to the “Piping Construction Engineering Manager”
* The current Piping Construction Engineering team size is 19 engineers; however, it also involves operational leadership of a matrixed team;
* As this is a front-line site delivery role, there is a necessity to work with flexibility and be able to work under the time pressure of the schedule in order to unblock technical issues to allow continuity of work by the installation teams.
* The Piping Completion Lead works closely with the installation Contract Engineering Lead and both reports to the Construction Engineering Manager who is part of a wider of team of Leaders delivering the E2E life cycle of the piping scope. Delivery of the upstream engineering sequence is outside the scope of the Construction Engineering team, however they should ensure integration with the other areas of the team and other disciplines.
* The Piping Completion Lead has counterparts across the other disciplines in MEH engineering, who perform equivalent roles for the other disciplines of MEH.
* The Piping Completion Lead will have delegation to perform decision making on site within a defined boundary to allow efficient and quick resolution of topics.
**Education, Experience and Skills:**
* Proven experience working in an equivalent / related role related to pressure test and completion activities;
* Meticulous and rigorous approach to engineering to achieve high professional standards;
* Proven ability to successfully deliver engineering safely to the correct quality, time and cost in a fast paced, schedule driven environment;
* Strong people leadership skills to coordinate efficient delivery of their scope through empowerment of their team members and drawing on the necessary support from others in the organisation;
* Ability to influence a diverse range of stakeholders;
* Ability to work autonomously but with awareness of own limitations;
* Knowledge of contractual and commercial mechanisms.
**Our Culture**
Our values stand on a foundation of safety, integrity, inclusion and diversity. We put people at the heart of our business, and we genuinely believe that we all succeed by supporting one another through our culture of caring. We value positive mental health and a sense of belonging for all employees. We aim to embed inclusion and diversity in everything we do. We know that if we are inclusive, we’re more connected, and if we are diverse, we’re more creative. We accept people for who they are, regardless of age, disability, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, mental health, race, faith or belief, sexual orientation, socioeconomic background, and whether you’re pregnant or on family leave. This is reflected in our wide range of Global Employee Networks centered on inclusion and diversity. We partner with VERCIDA to help us attract and retain diverse talent. For greater online accessibility, please visit www.vercida.com to view and access our roles. As a Disability Confident employer, we will interview all disabled applicants who meet the minimum criteria for a vacancy. We welcome applications from candidates who are seeking flexible working and from those who may not meet all the listed requirements for a role. If you require further support or reasonable adjustments with regards to the recruitment process (for example, you require the application form in a different format), please contact the team.

# Head of Data and Insight
**Lead data, insight and responsible AI transformation at Demelza** At Demelza, we believe better insight leads to better decisions, stronger services and greater impact for children and families.
We are looking for an experienced and ambitious **Head of Data and Insight** to lead our organisation-wide Data and Insight function at an important point in its development.
This is an opportunity to shape how Demelza uses data, analytics, automation and responsible AI across the organisation. You will lead a multidisciplinary team, turn our Data and Governance Strategy into practical delivery and help colleagues to use trusted evidence to support informed decision~~s~~ -making and demonstrate impact.
You will have the professional autonomy to set direction, establish priorities and build a modern, resilient data function. Just as importantly, you will see the direct connection between your work and Demelza’s mission to provide extraordinary care and support to children and young people with serious or life-limiting conditions and their families.
**What you will do**Reporting to the Director of IT, Data and Governance, you will:
* lead the implementation and continued development of Demelza’s Data and Governance Strategy;
* provide visible leadership, coaching and direction to the Data and Insight team;
* strengthen data quality, ownership, governance and reporting confidence across the organisation;
* develop our business intelligence and analytics capability, turning complex data into clear, actionable insight;
* oversee the development of organisation MI, dashboards, reporting models and our data warehouse;
* establish transparent priorities for data, reporting, systems and improvement requests;
* identify opportunities to improve processes, reduce duplication and make better use of organisational capacity;
* lead the safe, ethical and proportionate adoption of AI and automation;
* oversee a portfolio of data applications, integrations and system improvements; and
* work alongside senior leaders, trustees and colleagues across Demelza to translate evidence into practical action and measurable benefits.
**About you**
You will be an experienced data, insight, analytics or applications leader who combines strategic thinking with practical delivery.
You will bring:
* experience of leading and developing an effective data, insight, reporting or information governance function;
* a strong track record of translating strategy into prioritised plans, measurable outcomes and sustainable improvements;
* experience of leading organisational change, digital transformation or complex delivery programmes;
* experience of business intelligence, reporting and visualisation, including Power BI or comparable technologies;
* a good understanding of data quality, data governance, information security and responsible data use;
* confidence identifying and implementing appropriate automation and AI-enabled opportunities within a well-governed environment;
* strong people leadership skills and the ability to build capability, resilience and shared accountability;
* the credibility to influence senior stakeholders and constructively challenge assumptions;
* the ability to communicate technical or complex information clearly to different audiences; and
* a curious, collaborative and solutions-focused approach.
You do not need to have worked in a hospice before. Experience in healthcare, charities or another regulated environment would be valuable, but we are equally interested in the transferable knowledge, leadership and perspective you could bring.
Most importantly, you will be motivated by the opportunity to use data and technology for a clear social purpose.
## Why join Demelza?
This is more than a data leadership role. It is an opportunity to:
* shape the future direction of data, insight, automation and AI at Demelza;
* influence strategic and operational decision-making across the organisation;
* build a clear, supportive and organisation-wide data service;
* lead transformational work with visible and measurable impact;
* develop a talented multidisciplinary team;
* work with colleagues who care deeply about the quality and impact of their work; and
* use your expertise to support extraordinary care for children and families.
For an informal chat, please call Claire Ellis-Waghorn, Director of IT, Data and Governance, on 01795 845261. Closing date - **Monday 2nd November 2026** Interview date - **Wednesday 11th November 2026** Demelza greatly values the benefits of a diverse team and embraces diversity, equality, and inclusion in all areas of its work. We are committed to building a diverse and authentic workplace, ensuring that our team reflects the diversity of the children and families we support. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds.
To find out how we process your personal data during the recruitment process, please refer to the Employee Recruitment Privacy Notice.
As part of our commitment to safer recruitment, all offers of employment are subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, including a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at a level relevant to the role.
Demelza is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of children, young people and vulnerable adults and expects all employees and volunteers to share this commitment.
Demelza is an equal opportunities employer. Registered Charity No. 1039651.
## About Demelza
Demelza delivers extraordinary care to extraordinary children who are facing serious or life-limiting conditions, throughout Kent, South East London and East Sussex. We’re here to support them and their families at every step – from first diagnosis and for as long as we’re needed. Demelza believes in care that doesn’t back down. Benefits include:
* Generous annual leave, with buy/sell opportunities and length of service awards
* Enhanced maternity pay for eligible employees
* Opportunity to remain in NHS Pension
* Cycle to work scheme
* Tech scheme
* Eye care vouchers
* Wellbeing events and support
* Access to benefits and wellbeing platform
* Access to training and development opportunities

# Consultant
At Edge Health, we use data, economics and technology to solve difficult problems in healthcare and life sciences. We work with NHS organisations, government, life sciences companies and healthcare innovators on questions where good analysis can change a decision, a service or a policy. We are looking for a Consultant with 4+ years of professional experience, ideally in a consulting or healthcare analytics background to join our team full-time in London. You're someone who wants to lead projects and client relationships without moving away from the analytical work. Our consulting business focusses on both the delivery of projects to meet clients’ needs, and the development of repeatable propositions to take to market. Key skills and competencies we are looking for include:
* Experience planning projects and managing them on a day to day basis;
* Interest in building long-term client relationships and becoming a trusted adviser;
* Passion for working with healthcare data, and ideally experience of having done so;
* Technical skills and experience, such as data economics, statistics, coding, data science or modelling;
* Ability to work in a fast-paced environment; and
* Enthusiasm for working closely with our clients and partner organisations as well as with other members of the Edge team.
**What's it like to work at Edge?**
The role is deliberately a mix of consulting and analysis. At Consultant level you are senior enough to lead day-to-day client work and manage colleagues, but you are still expected to get into the substance, including: interrogating data, building or challenging a model, working with engineers and economists, and forming a view on what the analysis means.
The work is varied and often begins with a question rather than a prescribed method. We might be helping an NHS team redesign a service, evaluating the economics of a new technology, or building a tool that lets a client answer the question themselves. Because consulting, economics, data science and engineering sit closely together, people can move between these kinds of problems.
We are also small enough for people to shape what Edge does. Consultants can develop areas of expertise, start new propositions, publish work and test ideas outside client projects. We set aside two training days each quarter, and recent internal development time has produced new public tools as well as client propositions.
Edge is rated 4.9/5 on Glassdoor with 100% saying they would recommend the company. Recent reviews mention a supportive culture, interesting projects, personal development and lots of room to explore interests.
## Key Responsibilities
Key responsibilities within this role include:
* Project planning and management: Taking responsibility for the planning and management of consulting projects, overseen by a Senior Consultant or Director;
* Applying technical & industry expertise: Be a trusted and expert advisor to our clients in areas of technical (e.g. data science, health economics and modelling) or domain (e.g. healthcare and life sciences) expertise;
* People management: Managing a team of 2-4 colleagues within larger projects;
* Client management: Managing client expectations, writing update briefs for clients and presenting progress or outputs;
* Relationship-building: Building a strong network of clients and contacts within the health industry;
* Innovation: Proactively learning from past projects and experiences to build and develop new propositions for use within the health sector;
* Helping to win new work: Contributing to writing scope documents, bidding material and responses to tender requests;
* Business development: Supporting the wider growth of Edge, through development of marketing material and team training and development;
* Key account management: Taking on one or two key accounts with senior clients for whom we have delivered repeated propositions.
## Skills, Knowledge and Expertise
We greatly value diversity and would welcome applicants from a range of academic and professional backgrounds. While meeting all the stated job requirements can be beneficial, at Edge, we understand that diverse experiences and perspectives can bring great value to our work. So, if you're passionate about the work we do and share our values, we encourage you to apply, even if you don't meet every single criterion.
* At least 4 years of professional experience, working in a consulting, data, healthcare or closely-related setting;
* Experience of managing, coaching, training and developing less experienced colleagues and new hires;
* Experience of working day-to-day with clients or other organisations or teams in a professional setting;
* Domain knowledge in areas of healthcare, life sciences or related fields which you can bring to our clients as a trusted expert;
* Technical skills in the fields of data science, economics, engineering or statistics developed either through academia or professional experience;
* Be highly motivated, self-driven and versatile, and excited to work within a growing, entrepreneurial consultancy;
* Have the ability to engage effectively and enjoyably with a range of people, and to communicate impactfully the findings and implications of their work;
* Have a knowledge of languages such as SQL, R and Python, or a willingness and ability to learn how to do so quickly;
* Have experience of managing, planning and delivering projects and outputs to tight timescales and to a high quality;
* Take proactive responsibility for personal development, and the development of individuals and teams around them.
## Benefits
* Discretionary annual bonus (typically averaging ~10% of base)
* 25 days annual leave per year, including the option of buying up to 5 additional days.
* Vitality Private health insurance and/or Bupa Cashplan
* Two days training per quarter to support professional development
* Cycle2Work scheme
*We review applications on a rolling basis and invite candidates to interview as we go, so encourage you to apply early. If we receive a high number of strong applications, we may close the role before the advertised deadline.*
## About Edge Health
Edge Health is a boutique analytics firm of around 40 economists, data scientists and data engineers with backgrounds in economics, statistics, epidemiology, policy, management consulting and healthcare. We have worked for many years with NHS hospitals and policymakers, and are familiar with their challenges. We use new and diverse technologies centred around use of data to solve these issues at scale.
Since our formation in April 2017, we have grown rapidly and worked with more than 50 NHS organisations, including trusts, commissioners and regulators.
We are a client-facing organisation that sees the value in being close to the challenges we are helping to solve. We spend time working alongside our clients and enjoy seeing the direct impact of our work on patients and people who work in the NHS. Read more about the solutions we provide here.
We also have a passion for making our analysis accessible. We have used our technical capabilities to lead in the analysis of the COVID-19 pandemic, with our work reported on national and international networks. We also publish our analysis, where possible. Check out our blog here. *Edge Health is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion, and we welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates. As a Disability Confident Employer, we offer an interview to disabled applicants who meet the minimum criteria in the job description. Just let us know in your application if you'd like to apply under the scheme. If you need any adjustments at any stage, such as extra time for a task, a different application format or an accessible interview location, please get in touch.*

# Senior Data Engineer
We are hiring a data engineer to lead client delivery and build the next generation of engineers at Edge. This is a client-facing leadership role. You will spend most of your time working directly with both public & private organisations working in the healthcare sector, leading project teams drawn from every grade, and coaching junior engineers face to face. If the phrase “forward-deployed engineer” describes how you like to work, you will recognise this job.
The engineering matters, and you will need to be a capable engineer. What makes someone excel here, though, is the ability to operate with clients and to develop people. **What it's like to work at Edge**
The role is deliberately a mix of engineering and consulting. As a Senior Data Engineer you lead delivery with clients and develop the engineers around you, but you are still expected to be hands-on: building pipelines, making architecture calls, and noticing when a build is drifting from good practice. You'll work closely with economists, data scientists and consultants, so the engineering always connects to the question the client is trying to answer.
The work is varied and often starts with a problem rather than a spec. We might be building data infrastructure for an NHS organisation, bringing together sensitive patient data safely so it can inform decisions, or creating a tool a client can run themselves. Because we work across the public and private health sector, no two projects look quite the same.
We are also small enough for people to shape what Edge does. Senior Data Engineers coach junior colleagues, contribute to bids and proposals, and help set how we engineer as a team. We set aside two training days each quarter, and gaps in the stack are something we train rather than screen out.
Edge is rated 4.9/5 on Glassdoor with 100% saying they would recommend the company. Recent reviews mention a supportive culture, interesting projects, personal development and lots of room to explore interests.
## Key Responsibilities
Our projects are staffed with teams of mixed grades. Within them, you will:
* Plan and manage small and medium-sized projects, or the technical workstream of larger ones, supported by more senior colleagues;
* Produce client-ready output: pipelines, models, reports and presentations that can go in front of a client as they stand;
* Play an active part in client relationships: presenting, updating and handling harder conversations, with coaching from senior staff as you take on more;
* Develop the junior engineers on your projects, coaching them through client interactions and managing their delivery as well as the technical work;
* Handle sensitive data the way it should be handled, following our quality and information security practices, because being trusted with patient data is the foundation of everything we do;
* Help the junior engineers around you get better, sharing what you know with the team and supporting new joiners as they find their feet;
* Apply senior judgement to the technical work itself: noticing when a build is drifting away from good practice and doing something about it;
* Look for the moments where good delivery opens the door to more work, and flag them to the senior colleague leading the account as well as contribute to bids and proposals.
## Skills, Knowledge and Expertise
We greatly value diversity and would welcome applicants from a range of academic and professional backgrounds. While meeting all the stated job requirements can be beneficial, at Edge, we understand that diverse experiences and perspectives can bring great value to our work. So, if you're passionate about the work we do and share our values, we encourage you to apply, even if you don't meet every single criterion. The strongest applications will include examples of the following:
* You have delivered data work in a client-facing setting, such as consulting, an agency or an embedded role for 2-4 years, and are comfortable presenting your work and being challenged on it;
* You have started developing others, whether through mentoring, onboarding or day-to-day coaching, and can give us an example of someone who is better at their job because of you;
* You manage your own delivery well against deadlines and can plan and delegate work for a small team;
* You have solid engineering foundations: strong SQL, plus experience with some of Azure or AWS, Databricks and Terraform. Gaps in the stack are fine, and we will train them;
* You care about healthcare. Experience with the NHS or health data is a real advantage, and a passion for the sector is essential;
* You take your own development seriously, come to your one-to-ones ready to work on something, and act on the feedback you get;
* You are the kind of colleague people want on a project: straight with clients, considerate of the team, and someone who takes pride in working in the health & care sector;
* Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a technical discipline (computer Science, Engineering, mathematics or similar) expected.
## Benefits
* Discretionary annual bonus (typically averaging ~10% of base)
* 25 days annual leave per year, including the option of buying up to 5 additional days.
* Vitality Private health insurance and/or Bupa Cashplan
* Two days training per quarter to support professional development
* Cycle2Work scheme
*We review applications on a rolling basis and invite candidates to interview as we go, so encourage you to apply early. If we receive a high number of strong applications, we may close the role before the advertised deadline.*
## About Edge Health
Edge Health is a boutique analytics firm of around 40 economists, data scientists and data engineers with backgrounds in economics, statistics, epidemiology, policy, management consulting and healthcare. We have worked for many years with NHS hospitals and policymakers, and are familiar with their challenges. We use new and diverse technologies centred around use of data to solve these issues at scale.
Since our formation in April 2017, we have grown rapidly and worked with more than 50 NHS organisations, including trusts, commissioners and regulators.
We are a client-facing organisation that sees the value in being close to the challenges we are helping to solve. We spend time working alongside our clients and enjoy seeing the direct impact of our work on patients and people who work in the NHS. Read more about the solutions we provide here.
We also have a passion for making our analysis accessible. We have used our technical capabilities to lead in the analysis of the COVID-19 pandemic, with our work reported on national and international networks. We also publish our analysis, where possible. Check out our blog here. *Edge Health is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion, and we welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates. As a Disability Confident Employer, we offer an interview to disabled applicants who meet the minimum criteria in the job description. Just let us know in your application if you'd like to apply under the scheme. If you need any adjustments at any stage, such as extra time for a task, a different application format or an accessible interview location, please get in touch.*

## About the role
Junior Associate - Healthcare - Southampton
We are looking to attract a Junior Associate at all levels to join our Tier 1 Healthcare team in our Southampton office. Our Healthcare practice have just been awarded - Investors in People Gold, 2023. This is a team committed to engagement, high quality work, and outstanding performance.
The Team
Driven by the unprecedented demands of an ageing global population and growing levels of lifestyle-related chronic diseases around the world, the global healthcare sector is undergoing a period of rapid change.
Our multidisciplinary global healthcare group draws upon expertise across the firm and comprises of lawyers who specialises who specialise in litigation, coroner's inquests, the Court of Protection, capacity and consent, projects and construction, real estate, corporate, insurance, intellectual property, commercial, IT, regulatory and employment.
Our clients include public and private hospitals, pharmaceutical companies, insurance companies, healthcare suppliers and distributors as well as healthcare companies, private equity firms specialising in healthcare investments, health ministries and authorities.
Our extensive office network across the UK & Europe, US, Asia Pacific, Africa and the Middle East enables us to deliver a seamless integrated service to our healthcare clients around the globe.
This role is working with a partner who advises on a wide range of healthcare matters, including providing representation at inquests, representing clinicians before their regulatory body, medical device/product liability work and general advisory work.
Key Responsibilities
Applying strong technical skills and legal principles to a range of specific complex problems;
Drafting and interpreting complex legal documents using specialist knowledge;
Advising and counselling on claims involving breaches of professional standards;
Conducting legal discussions and liaising with clients and witnesses;
Presenting at seminars, writing for publications and hosting client events;
Understanding our client's business and identifying where the firm can help;
Preparing court documents;
Identifying opportunities and developing new or follow-on business;
Demonstrating an understanding of the global firm, its offices and practices and actively seeking out cross selling opportunities;
Understanding and dealing with client expectations, objectives, negotiating position and key concerns.
Essential Skills & Experience
Candidates will ideally have a minimum of 1 PQE. Please note that our PQE levels are a guide and all suitable candidates will be considered;
Display excellent legal skills and initiative, as well as managing and prioritising a full and varied caseload;
The ideal candidate will have significant relevant experience in defended clinical negligence practice including medical malpractice and experience dealing with multimillion pound matters;
The ideal candidate will have experience working within the healthcare sector;
The solicitors act 1974 requires practicing solicitors to have a practicing certificate; Successful completion of a Training Contract (or equivalent) and relevant education (Legal Practice Course; Graduate Diploma in Law (if non Law graduate); 2:1 honours degree or equivalent; A Levels)
We offer a nurturing and collaborative environment and agile hybrid ways of working in our offices. Our company benefits include 25 days holiday allowance plus the option to purchase more, pension scheme, health cash plan, life assurance and income protection. We also offer a number of discounts to use for gym membership, car leasing, mobile phones contracts and insurance products and a cycle to work scheme.
Clyde & Co is committed to promoting equality and diversity in all aspects of employment.
