At Optiver, the velocity of our software development is a critical part of our competitive advantage. Our ability to compete depends on how quickly new ideas can move from insight to production. The Developer Experience team is a strategic engineering function with a clear mandate: improve the development lifecycle across the company in ways that accelerate delivery and reduce our time to market. We build the tools, systems, and platforms that shape how software is developed at Optiver.
The Build Platform sits at the heart of that lifecycle. Every change an engineer makes flows through it. When builds are fast, correct, and reproducible, engineers stay in flow, receive fast and trustworthy feedback, and shipping changes becomes routine. When builds are slow or unreliable, every team in the company pays the tax, one slow feedback loop at a time.
We’re looking for a strong engineer with a passion for improving developer productivity, a deep interest in build systems, and the experience to design and operate platforms at scale. You’ll join a growing global Developer Experience team and help shape the future of how software is built, tested, and delivered at Optiver, enabling both engineers and agents to move from idea to production-ready software with greater speed and confidence.
What you’ll do
Shape the future of C++ builds at Optiver by designing and rolling out modern build systems that accelerate build times, improve reliability, and create a more consistent developer experience;
Develop common build libraries, reusable CI/CD pipelines, and container images used across the company;
Build observability into our platform so we can measure performance, reliability and adoption, and use that data to guide further improvements;
Improve build performance at scale through incremental execution, caching, dependency analysis and efficient scheduling;
Design workflows that enable agents to compile, test, diagnose failures, and validate changes reliably with minimal human intervention;
Work closely with engineering teams to understand where existing workflows create friction and turn those problems into scalable solutions;
Help teams adopt new tools and working practices, balancing standardisation with the needs of different codebases and engineering groups;
Stay current with industry trends and emerging tools in the developer experience and build systems space, helping guide our adoption of best-in-class solutions.
See the team lead's opinion on why DevEx matters here.
Who you are
You are a strong software engineer with deep experience in C++ build systems and developer tooling;
You have hands-on experience designing, adopting, or operating modern build systems such as Bazel, Buck2, Pants, or Gradle, ideally including migration from established tooling;
You have a deep understanding of build system concepts including incremental builds, caching, reproducibility, dependency graphs, remote execution, and artifact management;
You are skilled at diagnosing performance and reliability issues across the local development and continuous integration lifecycle, using data and observability to guide improvements;
You have significant experience with CI/CD platforms such as GitHub Actions, Buildkite, Jenkins, or similar, and understand how to design reliable, scalable pipelines and the infrastructure that supports them;
You hold a deep understanding of the end-to-end lifecycle of software development from ideation to deployment;
You have experience building tools and workflows around source control platforms such as GitHub and GitLab;
You are passionate about developer productivity and have a track record of delivering meaningful improvements to the software development lifecycle.
Who we are At Optiver, our mission is to continuously improve the market. By providing liquidity and accurate pricing in various financial instruments, to multiple exchanges across the world, we participate in the safeguarding of healthy and efficient markets.
What you’ll get You’ll join a culture of collaboration and excellence, where you’ll be surrounded by curious thinkers and creative problem solvers. Motivated by a passion for continuous improvement, you’ll thrive in a supportive, high-performing environment alongside talented colleagues, working collectively to tackle the toughest problems in the financial markets.
In addition, you’ll receive:
A performance-based bonus structure, enabling all of our employees to benefit from our global profit pool.
27 paid vacation days plus all UK public holidays.
Daily breakfast and lunch, along with support on commuting expenses.
Private medical insurance, pension scheme, and ClassPass fitness membership.
Training and continuous learning opportunities, including access to conferences and tech events.
International transfer opportunities for global career growth.
How to apply:
Apply directly via the form below. If you have any questions feel free to contact our Recruitment team via our recruitment inquiry form. Please note, we cannot accept applications via email for data protection reasons. Kindly note that we do not require assistance from third-parties including agencies in the recruitment of this role.
Diversity statement:
Optiver is committed to diversity and inclusion.

PJA is seeking an enthusiastic Engineering Geologist/Geotechnical Engineer to join our Ground Engineering and Contaminated Land Team, based in Birmingham.
We would also consider a senior engineer with similar credentials. The successful candidate will form part of a team of geologists, geotechnical specialists and geo-environmental consultants who pride themselves on being able to offer robust assessments relating to geotechnical considerations and soil and groundwater contamination. In conjunction with the wider engineering team at PJA, we provide a diverse range of services from preliminary due diligence assessments associated with land acquisitions, to the design and oversight of effective holistic ground solutions to enable the development of both brownfield and greenfield sites for a range of clients. The successful candidate should ideally have between 3 and 6 years’ relevant post-graduate experience and should be able to demonstrate a grounding in consultancy. A keenness to learn about all areas of geotechnical assessment, and an interest in geo-environmental engineering and their interface with land development is crucial. The responsibilities for this position are anticipated to include, but are not limited to the following: * Preparation of Phase 1 Desk Studies and completion of site walkovers;
* Design, procurement and monitoring of site investigations, including managing contractors;
* Soil sampling and logging in accordance with relevant standards.
* Gas and groundwater monitoring and sampling;
* Scheduling of chemical and geotechnical laboratory testing;
* Critically reviewing contractors’ factual data and reports;
* Preparation of Phase 2 geo-environmental interpretative reports;
* Preparation of geotechnical reports in accordance with CD622: Managing Geotechnical Risk
* Develop geotechnical ground models for use in design;
* Appraisal of potential ground engineering constraints;
* Preparation of preliminary foundation zoning plans;
* Providing input to earthworks specifications;
* Monitoring earthworks construction;
* Preparation of Earthworks Validation Reporting;
* Assisting with preparation of fee proposals for clients;
* Preparation of site-specific health and safety risk assessments for site work;
**The ideal candidate**
The ideal candidate should have experience in the use of ground investigation data management software such as Openground and have excellent MS Word and Excel skills. Some experience of AutoCAD and/or GIS software is also beneficial. The successful candidate will be required to prepare clear and concise technical reports and other written communications, and they should be able to demonstrate that they can achieve this to a high standard, while demonstrating good organisational skills and working to tight deadlines. Verbal communication is also of key importance, and the successful candidate will be able to confidently communicate with peers, mentor junior staff, and communicate with more senior colleagues, contractors and internal and external clients. Good commercial awareness is required to ensure work is undertaken within the time allowed and within budget, some project management experience would be beneficial. Applicants will ideally have membership of a professional organisation such as the Geological Society of London or the ICE and should be demonstrating an ongoing commitment to Continuing Professional Development and be working towards chartership. This is a permanent, full-time position based in our Birmingham office, however the candidate must have a willingness to regularly travel to and from sites around the UK for site work and meetings. Occasional overnight travel may be required. **As a member of the PJA team, you can expect:** * An attractive and modern working environment with good accessibility by all modes of transport
* The opportunity to progress quickly within the firm
* A wide range of challenging projects
* Ongoing support, training and mentoring from senior professionals within the business with a real commitment from senior management towards personal and professional development
**We also offer an attractive benefits package that includes:** * Competitive salary
* 25 Days annual leave plus the ability to purchase additional days
* Hybrid working arrangements
* Option to participate in the Company Share Ownership scheme
* Private healthcare
* Cycle to Work Scheme
* Techscheme
* Payment of professional subscription
* Membership of our group pension scheme
* Life Assurance
**How to Apply** If you would like to be considered for a role with us, then please email your CV and a covering letter to **recruit@pja.co.uk**. Please ensure you state the role/grade you are applying for in the email subject.

Company Description
Turner & Townsend is a global professional services company with over 22,000 people in more than 60 countries.
Working with our clients across real estate, infrastructure, energy and natural resources, we transform together delivering outcomes that improve people’s lives. Working in partnership makes it possible to deliver the world’s most impactful projects and programmes as we turn challenge into opportunity and complexity into success.
Our capabilities include programme, project, cost, asset and commercial management, controls and performance, procurement and supply chain, net zero and digital solutions.
We are majority-owned by CBRE Group, Inc., the world’s largest commercial real estate services and investment firm, with our partners holding a significant minority interest. Turner & Townsend and CBRE work together to provide clients with the premier programme, project and cost management offering in markets around the world.
Please visit our website: www.turnerandtownsend.com
Job Description
Owing to continued demand and our ambitious plans for growth, Turner & Townsend are looking to recruit Cost Intelligence, Data & Benchmarking professionals to enhance our capability in providing evidence‑based, data‑driven commercial insights across major infrastructure programmes. The role focuses on leveraging project, portfolio and market cost data to improve affordability, predictability and performance across capital infrastructure investment. You will support clients in making informed decisions across the full asset lifecycle — from business case and option selection through delivery, assurance and portfolio optimisation.
The North East & Yorkshire region has been successful in securing a number of long term frameworks supporting a wide range of major programmes and portfolios of work. We are flexible on location, these opportunities are available across the region within our Newcastle, Teesside, Sheffield and Leeds offices.
You will be making the difference for our clients by supporting them as an embedded resource within their organisation or through ad-hoc pieces of work for multiple clients across the Infrastructure sector as part of Turner & Townsend. Although our work is predominantly for regionally based clients, as workload requires, our people have the opportunity to work remotely (within region) on tasks for our clients both nationally and internationally.
Key responsibilities:
Develop, maintain and evolve infrastructure cost benchmarks across a range of sectors;
Analyse cost performance across assets, programmes and portfolios;
Identification of key cost drivers, trends and systemic variances;
Assist with the gathering and sharing of estimating data;
Support the automated capture, standardisation and governance of cost data across infrastructure programmes;
Work closely with Digital, Data and Innovation teams;
Support development and promotion of good practice within Turner & Townsend;
Assist in the achievement of departmental objectives;
Staying abreast of developments within own technical area of expertise to be able to give best practice advice in line with business objectives.
Key skills:
Strong understanding of infrastructure cost structures and delivery models;
Experience working with cost data, benchmarks and analytics on large or complex programmes;
Ability to identify meaningful insights from complex datasets;
Commercial awareness of infrastructure markets.
Qualifications
Experience in infrastructure cost management, cost intelligence, benchmarking or data analytics;
Background in consultancy, client‑side infrastructure organisations or major contractors preferred;
Degree in Quantity Surveying, Engineering, Economics, Construction Management, Data Analytics or similar;
Progress towards or membership of a relevant professional body (e.g. RICS) desirable.
Additional Information
Our inspired people share our vision and mission. We provide a great place to work, where each person has the opportunity and voice to affect change.
We want our people to succeed both in work and life. To support this we promote a healthy, productive and flexible working environment that respects work-life balance. Turner & Townsend is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and actively encourage applications from all sectors of the community.
Please find out more about us at www.turnerandtownsend.com/
